# Placeholder for the mosquitto password file.
#
# DO NOT commit the real passwd file. install.sh generates it on first run
# (`server` = the Pi server, `sp-3p` = smart plugs) with random passwords
# stored in the repo-root .env; each ESP32 node gets its own user from
# ./scripts/add-node-mqtt-user.sh <node_id>. Firmware nodes read their
# password from NVS (set via the captive portal on first boot).
#
# On Linux the real file is owned by the broker's uid 1883 (mode 0600) —
# mosquitto opens it after dropping privileges — so edit it with the scripts
# (they run mosquitto_passwd inside the broker image), not by hand:
#   ./scripts/add-node-mqtt-user.sh <node_id>     # add / re-key one node
#   ./scripts/rotate-mqtt-creds.sh [server|sp-3p|sp-cmd|sp-telemetry]
